\description{
The colours live on \code{layout.coloraxis}, so changing them needs no redraw.

The Axes tab's lines would otherwise fall on the strips that carry the figure's main
axes, so they are moved onto the heatmap here. Passed through \code{fixed.axes}, which
\code{\link[=.sci_finalize_plotly]{.sci_finalize_plotly()}} applies after the shared styling.

Each panel has axes of its own, linked to the others by \code{matches}, so a shared axis
never makes one panel of several. The first axis on each side goes to the outermost
panel, where its labels belong: the columns' under the bottom strips, the samples'
beside the right-hand strips. Those are the two axes the Axes tab styles.

The draw step of \code{\link[=methylationTrack]{methylationTrack()}} and its module. Colours come afterwards, from
\code{\link[=.meth_apply_scale]{.meth_apply_scale()}}.
}
